                <link target="model" x="0" y="572" />
            </button>
            <button x="277" y="58" width="183" height="30" uid="27" appearance="opaque" background="#0CA0FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="Intro: Build Your Own Model!" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <popup x="-184" y="40" width="617" height="346" background="yellow" color="black">
                    <text_box font-family="Arial" font-size="16">If you haven&apos;t modeled before, watch our Build Your Own Personal Finance Model video to help you get started with using STELLA modeling software, available at http://clexchange.org/curriculum/dollarsandsense.asp. &#x0D;&#x0D;Choose from 3 options:&#x0D;&#x0D;(1) Use this blank STELLA page to build your own model from scratch. Everything you need is here (icons/buttons for building blocks, tables and graphs, text; Word menus to run and print...);  OR&#x0D;&#x0D;(2) Click on the &quot;Explore Simple Stock and Flow Model&quot; button to see the &quot;core&quot; pre-built stock and flow model (Go ahead and make changes -- insert new numbers, change names, add building blocks!);  OR&#x0D;&#x0D;(3) Click on the &quot;Explore Model Used in Lesson 5&quot; to explore a version of the actual model used in Lesson 3 (it&apos;s a bit more complicated, but everything in it is explained!). &#x0D;&#x0D;Start wherever you want! Play with it and have fun!&#x0D;</text_box>
                </popup>
            </button>
            <button x="140" y="1674" width="147" height="32" uid="28" appearance="opaque" background="red" color="white" style="square" label="Build Your Own Model " font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
